Q: User input Form alignment A: <p>I believe what is happening here is:</p>
<p>By putting <code>frame</code> on the <code>LabeledContent</code> means that the label part of the labeled content will also share a part of that frame. Since &quot;Tolerance&quot; is less wide than &quot;Search Value&quot;, the text field + picker for &quot;Tolerance&quot; is wider than the text field for &quot;Search Value&quot;.</p>
<p>If you put <code>.frame(width: 300)</code> on just the &quot;content&quot; parts of the labeled contents, it achieves the desired layout.</p>
<pre><code>LabeledContent(&quot;Search Value:&quot;) {
    TextField(&quot;&quot;, value: $searchValue, format: .number)

    .frame(width: 300)
}

LabeledContent(&quot;Tolerance:&quot;) {
    HStack {
        TextField(&quot;&quot;, value: $tolerance, format: .number)

        Picker(&quot;&quot;, selection: .constant(1)) {
            Text(&quot;foo&quot;)
                .tag(1)
            Text(&quot;bar&quot;)
                .tag(0)
        }
        .pickerStyle(.menu)
        .labelsHidden()
    }
    .frame(width: 300)
}
</code></pre>
